# NPDUs that cross a router (§6.2.2, §6.5): destination before source, the
# hop count after both, MAC addresses opaque and as long as their length.

# ReadProperty to MS/TP network 5, MAC 0x0a.
01 24 00 05 01 0a ff 00 05 07 0c 0c 00 00 00 01 19 55 => to 5:0a, hops 255, expects-reply; confirmed-request invoke 7 service 12 max-apdu 1476 segments unspecified body 0c000000011955
# Its answer, as the router forwards it: the source network added.
01 08 00 05 01 0a 30 07 0c 0c 00 00 00 01 19 55 3e 44 42 c8 00 00 3f => from 5:0a; complex-ack invoke 7 service 12 body 0c0000000119553e4442c800003f
# Router to router: to a BACnet/IP MAC (192.168.1.10:47808) on network 1,
# from network 5, one hop spent.
01 2c 00 01 06 c0 a8 01 0a ba c0 00 05 01 0a fe 00 05 08 0c 0c 00 00 00 01 19 55 => to 1:c0a8010abac0, from 5:0a, hops 254, expects-reply; confirmed-request invoke 8 service 12 max-apdu 1476 segments unspecified body 0c000000011955
# Who-Is broadcast on remote network 5 only.
01 20 00 05 00 ff 10 08 => to 5:*, hops 255; unconfirmed-request service 8
# An I-Am answering it, through the router: device 10, 480 octets, vendor 5.
01 08 00 05 01 0a 10 00 c4 02 00 00 0a 22 01 e0 91 03 21 05 => from 5:0a; unconfirmed-request service 0 body c40200000a2201e091032105
# One hop left: the next router delivers it and forwards it no further.
01 20 ff ff 00 01 10 08 => to global, hops 1; unconfirmed-request service 8
